\p{Each item is stated for an augmented virtual ∞-equipment \code{P} and proved with the VDC∞ API only. Discrete specializations are acceptance tests (\ref{at-ft-0001} covers all of them).}
\ol{
  \li{\strong{Representable horizontals} and the characterization of companions and conjoints by their unit/counit cells; \code{f_* ≃ g_*} implies \code{f ≃ g} vertically.}
  \li{\strong{Yoneda.} Koudenburg's Yoneda embeddings in augmented VDCs: a vertical \code{y : a → â} with the universal nullary/unary cell structure such that restriction along \code{y} induces equivalences of the relevant cell spaces \strong{(verify exact form)}. Existence of Yoneda embeddings is a \em{property} of \code{P} ("has Yoneda embeddings"), holding in \code{Cat} with \code{â} the presheaf category of the next universe (→ D-RT-12).}
  \li{\strong{Right and left extensions and liftings} of horizontals along horizontals (Kan extensions inside the equipment), with the pointwise/absolute distinction stated through restriction.}
  \li{\strong{Weighted limits and colimits} of a diagram \code{d : j → a} weighted by \code{W : j ⇸ k} (resp. \code{k ⇸ j}), as representability of the appropriate restriction; conical limits as the unit-weighted case; comparison with → \ref{dec-up-0004} (\ref{at-ft-0006}).}
  \li{\strong{Adjunctions.} \code{f ⊣ g} iff \code{f_* ≃ g^*}; the space of adjunction data over a given \code{f} is contractible or empty; mates.}
  \li{\strong{Monads} in \code{P} as in → D-RT-09; Kleisli and Eilenberg–Moore objects by universal property; monadicity in the formal sense (Street) where composites exist.}
  \li{\strong{Fully faithful / essentially surjective} vertical morphisms via companions; equivalences as vertical morphisms with a companion that is also a conjoint of an inverse.}
  \li{\strong{Absolute liftings} and the formal definition of limits in the vertical ∞-category through them (the Riehl–Verity form), compared with 4 (\ref{at-ft-0007}).}
}
